#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198048 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198406 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "804ee2d1-5590-534d-ae11-7d2c5614a9b1" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the Y-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "81b0b6e1-41c3-5329-806e-162b8b27b045" :question/math-academy-id "e-12466" :question/problem "The lamina $D = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\le x \\le y  ,\\, 0 \\le y \\le 1 \\big\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y) = x^2y.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nM_y = \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\lambda(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda(x,y) = x^2y .$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot {x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{x}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[{\\int }_{0}^{y}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot {[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{y}^{5}}{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{6}}{24}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198049 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198407 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "9294903c-1b4c-58b6-a878-7f2220ec763d" :question/math-academy-id "e-12470" :question/problem "A thin plate ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) with the mass density function ![](images/c0/c0d0201b0a62f579bda5a0f915306917aa8a5c4389a24113e117e440d9c03511.svg) is enclosed between the curve ![](images/3f/3f9fd6a1cd82be925e9cd60e432d5657d75467cfef850dfbee06c9ac21c9bffb.svg) and the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-axis  for ![](images/01/01a308920c67f405d19c7ec1d166d7eaae1eecf725682c06b641af3100227e26.svg) Find the moment of the plate about the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) with the mass density function ![](images/4d/4d8c20e2119a539d5d1c0b7f47eaf00a86a32d686bf99722c3088142aca8139a.svg) about the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-axis is given by\n\n![](images/a5/a5f456d5b63d88aa947d5b5c2cb7c01f470a439d52d53a66ac52082997a35a0c.svg)\n\nIn our case, ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](images/06/067543543031a1d8cb4ceb9a7901ad7db77629243adc6658d4a9eab3e98fe09f.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n![](images/4f/4f528e9bf70f0d505fd2b0619d333b4958a18cdb14b3407fab046d8ff3f00af2.svg)\n\nand ![](images/11/11b094b50ce359e4838a4dd22e2d560a047a87e5ef6101bcd9421c6a0ffceb7b.svg) \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n![](images/aa/aa8a470b6d56e6f327d5e4d5fbf7f90c807292acc35c11ffb925876f1072d7dc.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198238 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198364 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f7a06a8-0260-5b59-b3a5-c02ee03980d4" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Center of Mass of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/id #uuid "8199670b-efe4-537b-8f8a-228d567a0944" :question/math-academy-id "e-8182" :question/problem "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y) = x+y$ and is enclosed between the curve $y=x$ and the $x$-axis for $0 \\leq x \\leq 1.$ Given that the mass of the plate is $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ units and its center of mass is located at $( \\overline{x}, \\overline{y} ),$ what is the value of $\\overline{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overline{x},\\overline{y}) = \\left( \\dfrac{M_y}{m}, \\dfrac{M_x}{m} \\right),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\iint \\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_x = \\iint\\limits_D y \\, \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_y = \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](images/b8/b872242423692a20a9d50658c99d9e8cee7c9b2737fb96592bc2bc35b4f72c32.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\:0 \\le x \\le 1, \\: 0 \\le y \\le x \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda(x,y) = x+y.$ \n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot (x+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}xy+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}xy+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}(\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{M_x}{m} = \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{5}{24}\\right)}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)} = \\dfrac{5}{12}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198239 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198365 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "255c9985-5d85-5fd5-a2b9-c4752f04afac" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Centroid of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/id #uuid "37d7f2ae-90b0-5e6f-83c2-7cb21ed4f089" :question/math-academy-id "e-8183" :question/problem "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $x=\\sqrt{1-y^2}$ and the $y$-axis for $-1 \\leq y \\leq 1.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." :question/worked-solution "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area $A_D$ is given by $(x_c, y_c),$ where\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle x_c = \\dfrac{1}{A_D} \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\: \\textrm{d}A, \\qquad \n\\displaystyle y_c = \\dfrac{1}{A_D} \\iint\\limits_D y \\, \\: \\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](images/a7/a7992c54f85f85cab3d9f923b8daca62c410393b364d30bcfbf5cff5efc93bbd.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\le x \\le \\sqrt{1-y^2}, \\: -1 \\le y \\le 1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nA_D = \\dfrac12 \\cdot \\pi\\cdot 1^2 = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-1}^{1}1-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{[y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(1-\\frac{1}{3})-(-1+\\frac{1}{3})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419224 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198407 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18e66a3a-ed9b-555f-aa83-dceb0f6ab492" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419123} {:answer/id #uuid "192d3c16-9364-50ee-8e11-2c62b71bb468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419125} {:answer/id #uuid "3b18f40a-a58f-50a7-a5ea-ec198571d256" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419137} {:answer/id #uuid "74d484cf-0400-577a-95c1-c6802b27225a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419152} {:answer/id #uuid "ddf0b53c-37d5-5309-9225-20866b1ac7b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18e66a3a-ed9b-555f-aa83-dceb0f6ab492" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419123} :answer-field/id #uuid "be411d10-9b35-59b2-bea4-598eab3d1363" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0804629b-6c24-5f03-92bb-4a1347fc49ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-162973" :question/problem "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,y\\le x\\le 2}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{2}\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2y[{\\int }_{y}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2y\\cdot {[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{x=y}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2y\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{y}]\\text{ }\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2-y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[2y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =(4-2)-(2-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419241 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198407 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "437edff8-59ef-5974-97e0-dc88d3352f3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419139} {:answer/id #uuid "8e2d61c3-5f92-5d5a-8848-72eb9b32bf48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419169} {:answer/id #uuid "b7fbe416-62db-5ea1-90c0-a62b49ebf492" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419178} {:answer/id #uuid "f58c447a-bfed-57d4-aa60-2857e9dedf35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419198} {:answer/id #uuid "fd07ae64-b7b6-5f33-96b4-d7d6cd7d0679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e2d61c3-5f92-5d5a-8848-72eb9b32bf48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419169} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e430080-5d22-5535-84c2-a8ad7d37f200" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419212}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "db64ad9a-61d4-5ef8-8403-3020448e1ff0" :question/math-academy-id "q-162978" :question/problem "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}$ is enclosed between the lines $x=y$ and  $x=4-y$ for $1\\le y\\le 2.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type II plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](images/1e/1e0f4ff99aecd563d03f19f5d6a2ede10610ac7117048d2c0d229dbb9c05651c.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\le x\\le 4-y,\\,1\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{4-y}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=y}^{x=4-y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}[(4-y)^{2}-{y}^{2}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(16-8y+{y}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}8-4y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[8y-2{y}^{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =(16-8)-(8-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419234 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198407 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caa24cd8-e361-5d5c-bd68-cce5193c2a96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419183} {:answer/id #uuid "d79e3d99-819f-52f6-be27-9b35ef393406" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419189} {:answer/id #uuid "f2cf2294-5376-5654-9423-3c12d8f0569b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419196} {:answer/id #uuid "f84ab0b2-467f-524c-882a-4876e0a9fdbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419201} {:answer/id #uuid "f97e15df-ec9c-51c0-9382-de16aec47732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2cf2294-5376-5654-9423-3c12d8f0569b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419196} :answer-field/id #uuid "f759501f-c45a-5f7a-bf9b-32c176d77fee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e0b4e86-c1ad-51fd-8e63-09fcf1f8e1c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-162980" :question/problem "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}$ is enclosed between the curve $y={e}^{x}$ and the line $y=e$ for $0\\le x\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](images/26/268322576d74a9d63d05e06f55011796e17c2b4ea7a96f583270b5c1cbdb14fb.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{e}^{x}\\le y\\le e}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{4}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{e}\\frac{4}{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4[\\operatorname{ln}⁡y]_{y={e}^{x}}^{y=e}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4-4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[4x-2{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =4-2-0 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198406 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "804ee2d1-5590-534d-ae11-7d2c5614a9b1" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the Y-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55ee8d50-fda2-5695-aec0-39df5d664378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419145} {:answer/id #uuid "70def251-0cf8-5748-8457-12451c6a03ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419151} {:answer/id #uuid "781bba58-5f0b-5b02-8f0b-ec472d6dfafb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419156} {:answer/id #uuid "820745d2-4e7c-5b27-ba28-06c134b98c36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419161} {:answer/id #uuid "bcd7a458-15cd-5d9b-9dd9-8890102867d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70def251-0cf8-5748-8457-12451c6a03ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419151} :answer-field/id #uuid "20f661b8-95f2-5f56-ab9f-c28fa283cf24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d1ae976a-0923-5524-b48c-beb7b491487b" :question/math-academy-id "q-162982" :question/problem "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{y}$ is enclosed between the line $x=y$ and the curve  $x=\\frac{4}{y}$  for $1\\le y\\le 2.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type II plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](images/16/163575c9a1adc54e1ccda5c3008e69413c44015596146bb435a528c4159abaa9.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\le x\\le \\frac{4}{y},\\,1\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{4/y}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}[{\\int }_{y}^{4/y}x\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=y}^{x=4/y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{y}[\\frac{8}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8}{{y}^{3}}-\\frac{y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =[-1-1]-[-4-\\frac{1}{4}] \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198407 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "020556d4-2945-5f3c-aaf3-c713eaecc1c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419117} {:answer/id #uuid "2896988c-89d0-54b8-bf68-e73ebca1c9af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419129} {:answer/id #uuid "33c751b9-2e87-53ae-a307-21577f2d2e24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419135} {:answer/id #uuid "407f253f-5a16-5d87-a64e-be5b12f2d748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419138} {:answer/id #uuid "81881644-86fe-52b8-bc64-3c2f14198487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81881644-86fe-52b8-bc64-3c2f14198487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419160} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6847620-7d7d-51f6-aec0-19d5ade74802" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "11cc651a-be53-58b2-a4ee-ca7bbf5bb71b" :question/math-academy-id "q-162985" :question/problem "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=15xy$ is enclosed between the curve $x=\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}$ and the $y$-axis  for $0\\le y\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type II plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](images/98/98a791c71bcad80b4e8427f1b2a311e1712fdbc8697d0475b2470c8e0281e8c5.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}},\\,0\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=15xy.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 15xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}15x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}15x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}x\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{y}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{15{y}^{2}}{2}(1-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{15}{2}{y}^{2}-\\frac{15}{2}{y}^{4}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{5}{2}{y}^{3}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{5}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198652 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198407 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5354ce0-11fe-543f-bd05-8141997dcf0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194544} {:answer/id #uuid "0cbf4653-eade-5469-8aeb-d16656acda9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194545} {:answer/id #uuid "342526d3-fc92-5eb0-9b17-c088df1aefe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194546} {:answer/id #uuid "4fca86e9-6fb0-5705-b29f-f8af6228793c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194547} {:answer/id #uuid "591a4e65-cc97-596a-9556-224c589303c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "342526d3-fc92-5eb0-9b17-c088df1aefe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194546} :answer-field/id #uuid "d62d4f76-fe82-58db-923e-00b5fd32b9a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16cb288f-0834-5fc0-aeb2-8e60e969c12a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163054" :question/problem "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=x{y}^{2}$ is enclosed between the curve $x={y}^{2}$ and $y$-axis for $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type II plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](images/34/34c6fb2eead75cb5217e7b33b5b98400b3f82e8ec29c91de9b8db5b22cefa6d7.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2},\\,-1\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=x{y}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{y}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}x\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{y}^{3}\\cdot {[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x={y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{y}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{{y}^{7}}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{8}}{16}]}_{y=-1}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}-\\frac{1}{16} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419238 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198406 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "804ee2d1-5590-534d-ae11-7d2c5614a9b1" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the Y-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a8f6e18-823f-5e94-bc82-b1869d75fd82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419167} {:answer/id #uuid "9ece2fe0-6b70-51a4-8981-b11680856300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419172} {:answer/id #uuid "ccfd0814-34ab-5875-a3df-47826dff5279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419184} {:answer/id #uuid "da8b8ee5-f2b9-50e8-bc2f-db8b1b184aad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419190} {:answer/id #uuid "f540c707-45ec-5408-84cd-b6c38eaa61a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da8b8ee5-f2b9-50e8-bc2f-db8b1b184aad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419190} :answer-field/id #uuid "c865a6cd-2270-5291-a329-e06e5401b586" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419220}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6f84ebc-ad2c-5b3f-b0ba-33fe56e0e4fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-163065" :question/problem "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le (x+1)^{3}}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x{y}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{(x+1)^{3}}x{y}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{1}^{(x+1)^{3}}{y}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot [3{y}^{1/3}]_{y=1}^{y=(x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3x(x+1-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419231 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198406 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "804ee2d1-5590-534d-ae11-7d2c5614a9b1" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the Y-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4686b8ca-0dda-57ce-bcde-92a9b5e1f3b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419141} {:answer/id #uuid "487b9982-583c-58cd-b11f-4c5c1fffcb32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419142} {:answer/id #uuid "a5e2ea0c-478b-5311-a197-200b8eb7dc19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419174} {:answer/id #uuid "c4aa1303-3c46-5c55-a55f-682d5367bec8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419182} {:answer/id #uuid "db8f2016-1983-59a6-b384-aa89f99c1ab1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db8f2016-1983-59a6-b384-aa89f99c1ab1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419191} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4bc44f2-d15b-53f9-bc69-5de0f2aa0a2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419219}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "70b8cc23-612e-5ff7-9483-d405ee51660f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163069" :question/problem "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,x-1\\le y\\le 1}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{x-1}^{1}\\frac{y}{x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}[{\\int }_{x-1}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=x-1}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2x}\\cdot [1-(x-1)^{2}]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{2x}(2x-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}1-\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(2-1)-(1-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198406 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "804ee2d1-5590-534d-ae11-7d2c5614a9b1" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the Y-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "672f119b-10c6-5226-9ed1-7d312226819b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419147} {:answer/id #uuid "6e9ccd49-054b-52ab-b058-322651023c06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419150} {:answer/id #uuid "76a0421e-c793-56de-a742-250612940bdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419154} {:answer/id #uuid "c23dacfc-cf2a-500e-9738-9e65fdee4ce3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419181} {:answer/id #uuid "d1428714-85eb-5f8c-802f-207055657d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c23dacfc-cf2a-500e-9738-9e65fdee4ce3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419181} :answer-field/id #uuid "40770567-80e2-5b25-94c2-60048a1a80b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "601852dd-a274-52fe-84a0-07108a3a4d6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163157" :question/problem "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}$ is enclosed between the line $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi x}{4}$ and the $x$-axis for $0\\le x\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](images/47/4730100420adb07f9ac2d4e9e6a67a8a1c299ef552b25af1163909631d260495.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi x}{4}}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\pi x/4)}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\pi x/4)}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot [\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y]_{y=0}^{y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\pi x/4)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(\\frac{\\pi x}{4}-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\pi {x}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{\\pi {x}^{3}}{12}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419237 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198364 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f7a06a8-0260-5b59-b3a5-c02ee03980d4" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Center of Mass of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1475a5d8-ebb1-57a2-8ab0-c696f4771a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419122} {:answer/id #uuid "36423f9c-3108-5219-8b40-d38797e07b08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419136} {:answer/id #uuid "67d4e3ce-55b3-5aff-9aa4-dff19e8ff2ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419148} {:answer/id #uuid "76ca467e-a2e1-5f88-9af3-dda072a634a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419155} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a46906-9912-568a-b4a7-3b9ef0bc2562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8a46906-9912-568a-b4a7-3b9ef0bc2562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419202} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1b549ea-c59d-5ced-9fac-4fd9794dd23f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a3000550-9bb9-5fcb-96d7-edd002b477b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-163209" :question/problem "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-y\\le x\\le 0,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}$ and has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)={x}^{2}y.$ Given that the mass of the lamina is $\\frac{1}{15}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot {x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{0}{x}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[{\\int }_{-y}^{0}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{x=-y}^{x=0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot (0-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-\\frac{{y}^{5}}{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{y}^{6}}{24}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{24})}{(\\frac{1}{15})}=-\\frac{5}{8}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419236 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198364 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f7a06a8-0260-5b59-b3a5-c02ee03980d4" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Center of Mass of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12fafcf1-b2e0-57a4-81c7-814718dac5dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419120} {:answer/id #uuid "87923468-c8f1-5ad2-9717-0e22874873a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419165} {:answer/id #uuid "972daaf7-40cd-5e54-a513-23c92ee4769b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419171} {:answer/id #uuid "b45015cd-4e2a-5cb0-89ea-6115a438ac21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419177} {:answer/id #uuid "d04b3f50-aef5-549a-9547-70e78bc1f210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "972daaf7-40cd-5e54-a513-23c92ee4769b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419171} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b70242e-f79b-565c-a0a7-d4e08191e680" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "966f4f78-b371-5721-ac9e-2f7135cb240b" :question/math-academy-id "q-163210" :question/problem "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi x}{4}}$ and has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}.$ Given that the mass of the lamina is $\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x/4)}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x/4)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot [\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y]_{y=0}^{y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x/4)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(\\frac{\\pi x}{4}-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\pi {x}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{\\pi {x}^{3}}{12}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419230 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198364 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f7a06a8-0260-5b59-b3a5-c02ee03980d4" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Center of Mass of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e874657-6312-5175-b6d0-b49b0a871aae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419131} {:answer/id #uuid "7d856fae-a626-5475-a8d8-cd0dcef0d49a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419159} {:answer/id #uuid "84956135-ce16-5de1-81df-df43434d2267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419162} {:answer/id #uuid "85151eab-63b6-50af-a3d3-0aa04e53463a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419163} {:answer/id #uuid "adaf1fb1-a76c-5693-8d27-f499b09baa75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84956135-ce16-5de1-81df-df43434d2267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419162} :answer-field/id #uuid "8103ab94-36ed-52b5-a141-f85c6f324589" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67539bda-8c11-5bde-87f2-4a2aeb72eb01" :question/math-academy-id "q-163211" :question/problem "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2-y,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}$ and has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=xy.$ Given that the mass of the lamina is $\\frac{2}{3}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-y}x\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2-y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}(2-y)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{y}^{2}-2{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{4}+\\frac{1}{10}{y}^{5}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}-8+\\frac{16}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{8}{15})}{(\\frac{2}{3})}=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419225 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198364 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f7a06a8-0260-5b59-b3a5-c02ee03980d4" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Center of Mass of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18fd15cc-d805-535c-b3cb-7da8c1935947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419124} {:answer/id #uuid "27d5934e-dfa3-51a3-aaa8-47a015d8c83e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419128} {:answer/id #uuid "463e3a11-a0ca-53b1-822c-d2a5fd1ac4b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419140} {:answer/id #uuid "4ed3dc9b-a405-5284-99cd-5c1bfc42cb3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419144} {:answer/id #uuid "78d0fe95-8b02-5ef6-8484-4f93641c9235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18fd15cc-d805-535c-b3cb-7da8c1935947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419124} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9b9b2b2-2793-52af-9037-ca02cdc38bd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419222}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0843dc47-16bf-5a44-aad9-6ea0121c3046" :question/math-academy-id "q-163212" :question/problem "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and is enclosed between the curve $y=\\frac{4}{x}$ and the $x$-axis for $1\\le x\\le 2.$ Given that the mass of the plate is $2$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](images/e6/e6027dcb30cf0d638dc4472c40182ddf9bd85d52840d1268d00c4d3ecbc09abc.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{4}{x}}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ \n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4/x}y\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}[{\\int }_{0}^{4/x}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=4/x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}(\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}}-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =-1+4 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419232 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198364 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f7a06a8-0260-5b59-b3a5-c02ee03980d4" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Center of Mass of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "143505c2-ce61-5ca3-bcfd-7e4da4746709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419121} {:answer/id #uuid "29a6aa2b-a636-56fb-8875-ff6a81b2edb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419130} {:answer/id #uuid "ab202c7c-0ae8-5c06-b512-4860a2cbccea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419175} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e0fb37-3844-523d-acfd-65bf6dcf598e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419180} {:answer/id #uuid "f27b4908-a73f-5b6e-8086-b96554461d99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f27b4908-a73f-5b6e-8086-b96554461d99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419195} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1da24df-d2f5-5a09-b4d8-15e1940c4d8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419221}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "71382edc-4cf1-5c73-9402-821a7a44c741" :question/math-academy-id "q-163283" :question/problem "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=x-y$ and is enclosed between the curve $x=-y$ and the $y$-axis for $-1\\le y\\le 0.$ Given that the mass of the plate is $\\frac{1}{2}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](images/e0/e01f73436854c4d337f4fa1dfbb31645c99ccdccbd4e36ae5145305f8b7b4a1f.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le -y,\\,-1\\le y\\le 0}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=x-y.$ \n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot (x-y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}xy-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-y}xy-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{2}-x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=-y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2}+{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{3{y}^{3}}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3{y}^{4}}{8}]}_{y=-1}^{y=0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{8})}{(\\frac{1}{2})}=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198365 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "255c9985-5d85-5fd5-a2b9-c4752f04afac" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Centroid of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01cd82d5-f5f6-5657-8791-e77a91fb2d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419116} {:answer/id #uuid "12280b40-8986-52b3-bfac-624f24463742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419119} {:answer/id #uuid "8910be2d-c903-5108-beeb-ba291c1de864" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419166} {:answer/id #uuid "8be6365b-c54d-5232-b799-0b3d16cf8bec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419168} {:answer/id #uuid "feea253a-0b62-5e2b-bd23-1c7f385238b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01cd82d5-f5f6-5657-8791-e77a91fb2d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419116} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dc67489-67f2-5eec-9782-77ff229310df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419210}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66ace88b-9157-59ee-88b0-b41cdfb4067c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163285" :question/problem "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $x=\\frac{1}{y}$ and the $y$-axis for $1\\le y\\le 2.$ Given that the area of the plate is $\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,$ find the $y$-coordinate of its centroid." :question/worked-solution "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](images/e9/e9800a42aa3086abfc36a301e6771c838d5c9413b3c3f279ee1fc85096476d9a.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{y},\\,1\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nand ${A}_{D}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/y}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y{\\int }_{0}^{1/y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y[x]_{x=0}^{x=1/y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y(\\frac{1}{y}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}1\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}[y]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198365 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "255c9985-5d85-5fd5-a2b9-c4752f04afac" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Centroid of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "221311ad-1314-5543-9f34-67e6f2e673e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419127} {:answer/id #uuid "2fa0e110-8ccd-5f34-a220-bbe0a3cc6141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419133} {:answer/id #uuid "757a667f-b050-5f38-bae3-a357020693c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419153} {:answer/id #uuid "a4efe8f0-93c6-5796-bc7d-e865cf587d36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419173} {:answer/id #uuid "d66d64dc-f120-5c42-8214-0a03a23c7137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "757a667f-b050-5f38-bae3-a357020693c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419153} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eb59124-c898-5670-859e-bd2efa7d35fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "95f0f4f2-b0bf-58b3-a3af-ab5290540b1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163286" :question/problem "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $y={x}^{3}$ and the line $y=1$ for $0\\le x\\le 1.$ Given that the area of the plate is $\\frac{3}{4},$ find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." :question/worked-solution "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](images/99/99c35aa7510a45a0df32868964f4743f44aaff3bc3d0017ee0c9f9afb90e7750.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand ${A}_{D}=\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x[y]_{y={x}^{3}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x(1-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x-{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198365 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "255c9985-5d85-5fd5-a2b9-c4752f04afac" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Centroid of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "020ac850-b2cd-5d3f-bd80-a39b02f4b24f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e+1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419118} {:answer/id #uuid "3329eaae-f5c1-5758-92c7-1a9cea23b6d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{e-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419134} {:answer/id #uuid "5e4229af-d0d4-5076-88ba-23eee2a7affd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419146} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f1523d-b142-5e8d-b289-8cd0f7807eaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419193} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d29c15-2245-5bd8-a436-d5662f27abb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "020ac850-b2cd-5d3f-bd80-a39b02f4b24f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e+1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419118} :answer-field/id #uuid "37160079-1d22-586e-b2bb-805c465a3227" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e1f668b-3939-5382-8535-1d312c4ff48a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163287" :question/problem "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le {e}^{x}}.$ Given that the area of the lamina is $e-1$ square units, find the $y$-coordinate of its centroid." :question/worked-solution "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e-1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{x}}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e-1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y={e}^{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e-1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e-1}{[\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{e-1}\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{e+1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198365 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "255c9985-5d85-5fd5-a2b9-c4752f04afac" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Centroid of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cf8cda9-bac2-59d6-834e-42eb85ee56ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419126} {:answer/id #uuid "2f838587-bedf-57ba-827e-cbd56613a0a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419132} {:answer/id #uuid "6c6a9a5b-f0c5-5e2f-9c4a-c8c11ec65c93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419149} {:answer/id #uuid "85eb245d-5c2e-5cec-80de-c5f54620fb0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419164} {:answer/id #uuid "cdf2780f-c70f-5d37-815e-adaeb163cac4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdf2780f-c70f-5d37-815e-adaeb163cac4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419185} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f4cdb77-32fa-50a5-be10-c994eb721af2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d550a84-797a-542e-9e3e-d629d42af4fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-163288" :question/problem "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $y=\\sqrt{x}$ and the $x$-axis for $0\\le x\\le 4.$ Given that the area of the plate is $\\frac{16}{3},$ find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." :question/worked-solution "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](images/95/951eb7592df1645f8743817809c0d4604b779de6a3112f7fcaf6aca5f214f302.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}}\n$$\n\nand ${A}_{D}=\\frac{16}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}x{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}x[y]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{[\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}\\cdot \\frac{64}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419239 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198365 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "255c9985-5d85-5fd5-a2b9-c4752f04afac" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Centroid of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cf46668-7609-5992-8979-90c41bfd3fc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419143} {:answer/id #uuid "7d3df44e-fbd7-59bc-8f40-345b9246462d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419158} {:answer/id #uuid "94607412-6822-5182-bdcf-244d18e6c462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419170} {:answer/id #uuid "e6afa83f-bf20-5c8d-9c0d-02e968653c46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419194} {:answer/id #uuid "f702fa21-4534-5dd8-aab9-1ec26c5dad64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f702fa21-4534-5dd8-aab9-1ec26c5dad64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419200} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f5e3fa2-ce88-5fb7-b1ce-a349d55bc0e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b0dadff4-48ef-5038-93b5-63661b50e4ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-163502" :question/problem "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2y,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.$ Given that the area of the lamina is $9$ square units, find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." :question/worked-solution "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{[\\frac{2{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198406 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "804ee2d1-5590-534d-ae11-7d2c5614a9b1" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the Y-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9390295c-2047-55db-93f2-b19050e20819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197709} {:answer/id #uuid "b3514fe4-5f80-5a9c-bbdb-8de58bceec43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197710} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7fe96a-bf45-5c14-aaa0-a2d45935fcca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197711} {:answer/id #uuid "c745270c-8cff-50c9-b613-62dab171bf06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197712} {:answer/id #uuid "07a1a73a-6524-5480-bf7d-4a337f3b8641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9390295c-2047-55db-93f2-b19050e20819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197709} :answer-field/id #uuid "cda48d4b-6932-57c7-959c-1d532024e187" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "89fa45e3-9075-5e3c-bd26-a3b248d1b5cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-39534" :question/problem "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=4y$ is enclosed between the line $x=y$ and the $y$-axis for $1\\le y\\le 2.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type II plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](images/f8/f8454539cbe01d45842ab03386e06bbbdca35d400d0e214563843d99cddd5a85.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le y,\\,1\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=4y.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 4y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}4xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}4xy\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2y[{\\int }_{0}^{y}2x\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2y[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2y({y}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =8-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
